<title>USA: Portland, Conn., approves $16.97 mln budget -- paper.</title>
<headline>Portland, Conn., approves $16.97 mln budget -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portland, Conn., took less than 15 minutes to approve a $16.97 million town budget earlier this week, which is $472,434 above the 1997 spending plan, although the tax rate stays at 28.76 mills.</p>
<p>The approved budget was same as the one presented in the winter by First Selectman Edward Kalinowski.</p>
<p>Only a voice vote was required because there were no amendments, the paper said.</p>
<p>((--Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654))</p>
</text>
